{
  "_comment": [
    "Station CROSSWALK: feed-local names that must resolve to one canonical id.",
    "",
    "A cross-border journey only exists if both halves name the interchange the same",
    "way, and the feeds do not agree: SNCF publishes city aggregates ('PARIS",
    "(intramuros)'), while DB and SNCB name individual termini ('Paris Est', 'Paris",
    "Nord (FR)'). Most stations need no entry — the converter already unifies names",
    "that merely differ by accent, punctuation or a '(DE)' country tag. This file is",
    "only for genuine disagreements, so it stays short enough to keep correct.",
    "",
    "Keys are canonical ids (the SNCF label where one exists, so the French half of a",
    "join lands on the same node). Values are NORMALIZED feed names: lower-case, no",
    "accents, no country tag, punctuation collapsed to spaces — see normalizeStationName",
    "in scripts/fetch-networks.ts.",
    "",
    "An entry also PINS a station into every feed's allowlist, so a genuine border",
    "interchange is never ranked out for being quiet — Perpignan carries few trains",
    "but is where the French and Spanish networks actually meet."
  ],

